{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "PRO",
  "chapter": 9,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PRO.9.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.9.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wisdom hath builded her house;\nShe hath hewn out her seven pillars:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.9.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.9.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "She hath killed her beasts; she hath mingled her wine;\nShe hath also furnished her table:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.9.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.9.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "She hath sent forth her maidens;\nShe crieth upon the highest places of the city:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.9.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.9.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whoso is simple, let him turn in hither:\nAs for him that is void of understanding, she saith to him,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.9.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.9.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Come, eat ye of my bread,\nAnd drink of the wine which I have mingled.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.9.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.9.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Leave off, ye simple ones, and live;\nAnd walk in the way of understanding.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.9.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.9.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that correcteth a scoffer getteth to himself reviling;\nAnd he that reproveth a wicked man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "getteth",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " himself a blot.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.9.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.9.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Reprove not a scoffer, lest he hate thee:\nReprove a wise man, and he will love thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.9.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.9.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Give ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "instruction",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to a wise man, and he will be yet wiser:\nTeach a righteous man, and he will increase in learning.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.9.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.9.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The fear of Jehovah is the beginning of wisdom;\nAnd the knowledge of the Holy One is understanding.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.9.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.9.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For by me thy days shall be multiplied,\nAnd the years of thy life shall be increased.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.9.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.9.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If thou art wise, thou art wise for thyself;\nAnd if thou scoffest, thou alone shalt bear it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.9.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.9.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The foolish woman is clamorous;",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "She is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " simple, and knoweth nothing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.9.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.9.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And she sitteth at the door of her house,\nOn a seat in the high places of the city,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.9.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.9.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To call to them that pass by,\nWho go right on their ways:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.9.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.9.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whoso is simple, let him turn in hither;\nAnd as for him that is void of understanding, she saith to him,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.9.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.9.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Stolen waters are sweet,\nAnd bread ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "eaten",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in secret is pleasant.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.9.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.9.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But he knoweth not that the dead are there;\nThat her guests are in the depths of Sheol.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
